<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Tamrash</h1><p class="st-meta">1878 CE – 1886 CE · capital Tamrash</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Self-governing community of Muslim Pomak villages in the Rhodope mountains that refused Russian and Bulgarian rule after the war of 1877 to 1878.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1877 to 1878, Muslim Bulgarian-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomaks">Pomaks</a> in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodope-mountains">Rhodopes</a> resisted the advancing Russian army. After the war, about twenty villages around Tamrash refused to submit to the Russian administration or to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eastern-rumelia">Eastern Rumelia</a>, and organised their own defence and government in the mountains.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known mainly from diplomatic reports, the community was governed by local Muslim notables and village councils, under the nominal suzerainty of the Ottoman sultan. It survived because of its remote terrain and because the Great Powers left its status unresolved.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> absorbed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eastern-rumelia">Eastern Rumelia</a> in 1885, the Bulgarian-Ottoman agreement of 1886 transferred the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomaks">Pomak</a> villages and the Kardzhali district back to direct Ottoman rule. They became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a> of 1912 to 1913.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-tamrash.jpg" alt="Republic of Tamrash" width="320" height="368"><figcaption>Image: Chech Explorer; ANGELUS (File:Black star.png author); Brosen and Howcheng (File:Simple compass rose.svg authors) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Of_The_Republic_Of_Tamrash_EN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1878 CE – 1886 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tamrash</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bulgarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pomak Republic, Rhodope Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1882&amp;focus=republic-of-tamrash" aria-label="Republic of Tamrash on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5274 695 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Tamrash lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5594 951L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5594 951h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5594 951h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1882&amp;focus=republic-of-tamrash">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
